The "Subnormal" branch might not be reached when signed integer overflow. That is undefined behavior and permits compilers to aggressively optimize away what it assumes is unreachable code when exponent overflows.
```
  if (exponent > 308) {
    *error = ERANGE;
    return HUGE_VAL;
  } else if (exponent > 0) {
    number *= e[exponent];
  } else if (exponent < -308) { // Subnormal
    if (exponent < -616) {      // Prevent invalid array access.
      number = 0.;
    } else {
      number /= e[-308 - exponent];
      number /= e[308];
    }

  } else {
    number /= e[-exponent];
  }
```

